":{"id":112,"description":null,"name":"Reuters"},"teaserSnippet":"WASHINGTON, Jan 30 (Reuters) - President Donald Trump said on Friday it would be inappropriate to ask Kevin Warsh, his nominee to be the next chair of the Federal Reserve, whether he would cut interest rates, but added he was confident Warsh was inclined to lower borrowing costs.","legacyThumbnailImageUrl":null,"image":{"detail":{"default":{"srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a8c61b15-b8e3-48e2-a4b5-09fed9190dc1.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=1920\u0026token=aecf9139409e7a693a97c91f19bb1375301cb347cc641f082b29a4250becc371"},"sources":{"teaser_small":{"srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a8c61b15-b8e3-48e2-a4b5-09fed9190dc1.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=200\u0026token=3f162c342ab979c0b97c21e8bfbc215c330cc6812e93947dc32ae37326461638","media":"all and (min-width: 0px)"},"teaser_medium":{"srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a8c61b15-b8e3-48e2-a4b5-09fed9190dc1.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=400\u0026token=c5046785e0a604cad5ec6b77163085e661461c1b9eaaf2d95ad26b457f76eb1c","media":"all and (min-width: 0px)"},"desktop":{"media":"all and (min-width: 1024px)","srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a8c61b15-b8e3-48e2-a4b5-09fed9190dc1.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=1920\u0026token=aecf9139409e7a693a97c91f19bb1375301cb347cc641f082b29a4250becc371"},"mobile":{"media":"all and (min-width: 0px)","srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a8c61b15-b8e3-48e2-a4b5-09fed9190dc1.webp?top=0\u0026left=279.8353909465\u0026width=720.329218107\u0026height=720\u0026scale_width=768\u0026token=3f50ca3f7fea878953176b869cc08306911bc59f22df8fd9b7c3133099f33708"},"tablet":{"media":"all and (min-width: 768px)","srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a8c61b15-b8e3-48e2-a4b5-09fed9190dc1.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=1024\u0026token=32ddaa9c947a85f8f9f4fc2c83b772475c87c58e73b73531b9127007bb20d559"}}}},"featuredContent":null,"tags":[],"audioTts":null,"summaryBullets":[]},{"id":216950,"title":"Citi sees gold supported by risks, with some fading expected later in 2026","teaserHeadline":null,"urlAlias":"/news/off-the-wire/2026-01-30/citi-sees-gold-supported-risks-some-fading-expected-later-2026","createdAt":"2026-01-30T14:11:45-0500","updatedAt":"2026-01-30T14:17:38-0500","author":{"email":"legacy-642@kitco.com","name":"Reuters","imageUrl":null,"urlAlias":"/author/reuters"},"source":{"id":112,"description":null,"name":"Reuters"},"teaserSnippet":"Jan 30 (Reuters) - Gold investment allocations are being underpinned by a broad mix of overlapping geopolitical and economic risks, but around half of the risk may fade later this year, Citi said on Friday.Some of the core risks supporting gold demand - including U.S.-China tensions, China–Taiwan risks, concerns over U.S. government debt and uncertainty around artificial intelligence - were likely to keep prices elevated by historical standards, Citi said.","legacyThumbnailImageUrl":null,"image":{"detail":{"default":{"srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/852274e0-dbf7-4f10-ad77-fb757d6893c9.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=1920\u0026token=f39342a7cc13aa37167df14696a353eb5d54b0a81499d87cfca2b065efd6f58b"},"sources":{"teaser_small":{"srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/852274e0-dbf7-4f10-ad77-fb757d6893c9.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=200\u0026token=440ceaf4eeece7aaffa2651a4a708c7803d954e1de3328235b9ba982b9a06819","media":"all and (min-width: 0px)"},"teaser_medium":{"srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/852274e0-dbf7-4f10-ad77-fb757d6893c9.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=400\u0026token=bbebca913c5925ea0219ef10f0619085d3005d14d69a426e176c64b3d09d0281","media":"all and (min-width: 0px)"},"desktop":{"media":"all and (min-width: 1024px)","srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/852274e0-dbf7-4f10-ad77-fb757d6893c9.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=1920\u0026token=f39342a7cc13aa37167df14696a353eb5d54b0a81499d87cfca2b065efd6f58b"},"mobile":{"media":"all and (min-width: 0px)","srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/852274e0-dbf7-4f10-ad77-fb757d6893c9.webp?top=0\u0026left=279.8353909465\u0026width=720.329218107\u0026height=720\u0026scale_width=768\u0026token=bd59d9ee8e754fc8e94cfde0d56c10dc47be4b8a8bd81bcaefffd14a73ba1485"},"tablet":{"media":"all and (min-width: 768px)","srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/852274e0-dbf7-4f10-ad77-fb757d6893c9.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=1024\u0026token=d63b51cb5378e2215438e7c14fa7bbd0c8e629ae8be1bca13c2745edbde571ad"}}}},"featuredContent":null,"tags":[],"audioTts":null,"summaryBullets":[]},{"id":216948,"title":"Fed's Musalem says no more rate cuts needed with policy now at neutral level","teaserHeadline":null,"urlAlias":"/news/off-the-wire/2026-01-30/feds-musalem-says-no-more-rate-cuts-needed-policy-now-neutral-level","createdAt":"2026-01-30T14:05:13-0500","updatedAt":"2026-01-30T14:05:56-0500","author":{"email":"legacy-642@kitco.com","name":"Reuters","imageUrl":null,"urlAlias":"/author/reuters"},"source":{"id":112,"description":null,"name":"Reuters"},"teaserSnippet":"WASHINGTON, Jan 30 (Reuters) - St. Louis Federal Reserve President Alberto Musalem said on Friday ​the U.S. central bank does not ‌need to cut interest rates further unless the job market starts to deteriorate or inflation falls.The current 3.50%-3.75% policy rate range is neutral, ‌Musalem said in remarks prepared for delivery ​to an event at the University of Arkansas. With the economy expected to continue ‍growing above trend, there is no need to add monetary stimulus at a time when credit conditions ⁠and fiscal policy are both serving as \"tailwinds,\" ‍he added.","legacyThumbnailImageUrl":null,"image":{"detail":{"default":{"srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a38de551-3f2a-4d0d-b3a0-9fa10f80323c.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=1920\u0026token=a4cc24beca2b1b7322f6949364ac48c429e52ceb8d7cd28cc734cabcc3043381"},"sources":{"teaser_small":{"srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a38de551-3f2a-4d0d-b3a0-9fa10f80323c.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=200\u0026token=212eabf94122ea3d43443cc3d99869e5c81450b537bbdb9b9185ce44ee061ca0","media":"all and (min-width: 0px)"},"teaser_medium":{"srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a38de551-3f2a-4d0d-b3a0-9fa10f80323c.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=400\u0026token=23740b87fc21d3b1fec388cc94e85b6a435bdb05a52002fe07baebc79bb63db5","media":"all and (min-width: 0px)"},"desktop":{"media":"all and (min-width: 1024px)","srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a38de551-3f2a-4d0d-b3a0-9fa10f80323c.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=1920\u0026token=a4cc24beca2b1b7322f6949364ac48c429e52ceb8d7cd28cc734cabcc3043381"},"mobile":{"media":"all and (min-width: 0px)","srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a38de551-3f2a-4d0d-b3a0-9fa10f80323c.webp?top=0\u0026left=279.8353909465\u0026width=720.329218107\u0026height=720\u0026scale_width=768\u0026token=a5d45cfe2135881c8fc2059e5fb11d3d3ffc189f0187b132e0a1612f4f77faf3"},"tablet":{"media":"all and (min-width: 768px)","srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a38de551-3f2a-4d0d-b3a0-9fa10f80323c.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=1024\u0026token=e706bc8bddcbba07fe6d1c464bf0aa939cca0a50811c9e8683dcfcbd96bc07c4"}}}},"featuredContent":null,"tags":[],"audioTts":null,"summaryBullets":[]},{"id":216941,"title":"Trump advisor Hassett tells CNBC Warsh a good pick to run central bank","teaserHeadline":null,"urlAlias":"/news/off-the-wire/2026-01-30/trump-advisor-hassett-tells-cnbc-warsh-good-pick-run-central-bank","createdAt":"2026-01-30T12:29:56-0500","updatedAt":"2026-01-30T12:31:17-0500","author":{"email":"legacy-642@kitco.com","name":"Reuters","imageUrl":null,"urlAlias":"/author/reuters"},"source":{"id":112,"description":null,"name":"Reuters"},"teaserSnippet":"Jan 30 (Reuters) - Top White House economic adviser Kevin Hassett on Friday said the Federal Reserve blundered in ​not cutting rates this week, in comments that also called for ‌a swift approval of Kevin Warsh to be Fed Chair.Hassett, speaking on CNBC, acknowledged the legal issues that surround the Fed that could gum up any approval process until they are resolved.","legacyThumbnailImageUrl":null,"image":{"detail":{"default":{"srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/852274e0-dbf7-4f10-ad77-fb757d6893c9.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=1920\u0026token=f39342a7cc13aa37167df14696a353eb5d54b0a81499d87cfca2b065efd6f58b"},"sources":{"teaser_small":{"srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/852274e0-dbf7-4f10-ad77-fb757d6893c9.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=200\u0026token=440ceaf4eeece7aaffa2651a4a708c7803d954e1de3328235b9ba982b9a06819","media":"all and (min-width: 0px)"},"teaser_medium":{"srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/852274e0-dbf7-4f10-ad77-fb757d6893c9.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=400\u0026token=bbebca913c5925ea0219ef10f0619085d3005d14d69a426e176c64b3d09d0281","media":"all and (min-width: 0px)"},"desktop":{"media":"all and (min-width: 1024px)","srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/852274e0-dbf7-4f10-ad77-fb757d6893c9.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=1920\u0026token=f39342a7cc13aa37167df14696a353eb5d54b0a81499d87cfca2b065efd6f58b"},"mobile":{"media":"all and (min-width: 0px)","srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/852274e0-dbf7-4f10-ad77-fb757d6893c9.webp?top=0\u0026left=279.8353909465\u0026width=720.329218107\u0026height=720\u0026scale_width=768\u0026token=bd59d9ee8e754fc8e94cfde0d56c10dc47be4b8a8bd81bcaefffd14a73ba1485"},"tablet":{"media":"all and (min-width: 768px)","srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/852274e0-dbf7-4f10-ad77-fb757d6893c9.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=1024\u0026token=d63b51cb5378e2215438e7c14fa7bbd0c8e629ae8be1bca13c2745edbde571ad"}}}},"featuredContent":null,"tags":[],"audioTts":null,"summaryBullets":[]},{"id":216940,"title":"Fed's Miran assumes Warsh will fill his governor slot at central bank - CNBC ","teaserHeadline":null,"urlAlias":"/news/off-the-wire/2026-01-30/feds-miran-assumes-warsh-will-fill-his-governor-slot-central-bank-cnbc","createdAt":"2026-01-30T12:27:06-0500","updatedAt":"2026-01-30T12:29:34-0500","author":{"email":"legacy-642@kitco.com","name":"Reuters","imageUrl":null,"urlAlias":"/author/reuters"},"source":{"id":112,"description":null,"name":"Reuters"},"teaserSnippet":"Jan 30 (Reuters) - Federal Reserve Governor Stephen Miran said in a television interview Friday that he assumes Kevin Warsh, nominated to succeed current Fed chair Jerome Powell, will likely fill his expiring term at the central bank.Speaking on CNBC, Miran noted that his term, which ends on January 31, would be the only slot available for Warsh, himself a former Fed Governor, to take as part of the effort to install him as chair.","legacyThumbnailImageUrl":null,"image":{"detail":{"default":{"srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a1b24c45-3549-4749-8ff8-49b0b966f967.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=1920\u0026token=7ca387403b61a048ea98b4b3dc1e80b1a74563f4fcb6f8f7bbd79c22a3dcb815"},"sources":{"teaser_small":{"srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a1b24c45-3549-4749-8ff8-49b0b966f967.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=200\u0026token=9f79dc41ed3565c117dc137d2a2b69325c8717ba0b60b2e9c924d6f0d0ee1753","media":"all and (min-width: 0px)"},"teaser_medium":{"srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a1b24c45-3549-4749-8ff8-49b0b966f967.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=400\u0026token=20b2fb03d57e8b87dd08d95c35a2affc462adf34d7931f61efd12c6c39dc8113","media":"all and (min-width: 0px)"},"desktop":{"media":"all and (min-width: 1024px)","srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a1b24c45-3549-4749-8ff8-49b0b966f967.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=1920\u0026token=7ca387403b61a048ea98b4b3dc1e80b1a74563f4fcb6f8f7bbd79c22a3dcb815"},"mobile":{"media":"all and (min-width: 0px)","srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a1b24c45-3549-4749-8ff8-49b0b966f967.webp?top=0\u0026left=279.8353909465\u0026width=720.329218107\u0026height=720\u0026scale_width=768\u0026token=4efd11f95ab7bd6ea343bfa03103068aca48b6dbff89ca27b26ce3c86f21a925"},"tablet":{"media":"all and (min-width: 768px)","srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a1b24c45-3549-4749-8ff8-49b0b966f967.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=1024\u0026token=bb6d0cb5d4a0a9b39a331a04ea40833c895513d87b6f163d577d326ff4e7681e"}}}},"featuredContent":null,"tags":[],"audioTts":null,"summaryBullets":[]},{"id":216930,"title":"Global uncertainty, market correction risks cloud India's growth outlook, top adviser says","teaserHeadline":null,"urlAlias":"/news/off-the-wire/2026-01-30/global-uncertainty-market-correction-risks-cloud-indias-growth-outlook","createdAt":"2026-01-30T10:08:50-0500","updatedAt":"2026-01-30T10:10:22-0500","author":{"email":"legacy-642@kitco.com","name":"Reuters","imageUrl":null,"urlAlias":"/author/reuters"},"source":{"id":112,"description":null,"name":"Reuters"},"teaserSnippet":"NEW DELHI, Jan 30 (Reuters) - India's growth outlook faces potential downside risks from global macroeconomic uncertainty and prolonged financial market corrections, the country's chief economic adviser said days before the federal budget, with the economy on track to grow above 7% this fiscal year.","legacyThumbnailImageUrl":null,"image":{"detail":{"default":{"srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a1b24c45-3549-4749-8ff8-49b0b966f967.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=1920\u0026token=7ca387403b61a048ea98b4b3dc1e80b1a74563f4fcb6f8f7bbd79c22a3dcb815"},"sources":{"teaser_small":{"srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a1b24c45-3549-4749-8ff8-49b0b966f967.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=200\u0026token=9f79dc41ed3565c117dc137d2a2b69325c8717ba0b60b2e9c924d6f0d0ee1753","media":"all and (min-width: 0px)"},"teaser_medium":{"srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a1b24c45-3549-4749-8ff8-49b0b966f967.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=400\u0026token=20b2fb03d57e8b87dd08d95c35a2affc462adf34d7931f61efd12c6c39dc8113","media":"all and (min-width: 0px)"},"desktop":{"media":"all and (min-width: 1024px)","srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a1b24c45-3549-4749-8ff8-49b0b966f967.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=1920\u0026token=7ca387403b61a048ea98b4b3dc1e80b1a74563f4fcb6f8f7bbd79c22a3dcb815"},"mobile":{"media":"all and (min-width: 0px)","srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a1b24c45-3549-4749-8ff8-49b0b966f967.webp?top=0\u0026left=279.8353909465\u0026width=720.329218107\u0026height=720\u0026scale_width=768\u0026token=4efd11f95ab7bd6ea343bfa03103068aca48b6dbff89ca27b26ce3c86f21a925"},"tablet":{"media":"all and (min-width: 768px)","srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a1b24c45-3549-4749-8ff8-49b0b966f967.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=1024\u0026token=bb6d0cb5d4a0a9b39a331a04ea40833c895513d87b6f163d577d326ff4e7681e"}}}},"featuredContent":null,"tags":[],"audioTts":null,"summaryBullets":[]},{"id":216918,"title":"Gold, silver and copper tumble as nervous investors discover gravity","teaserHeadline":null,"urlAlias":"/news/off-the-wire/2026-01-30/gold-silver-and-copper-tumble-nervous-investors-discover-gravity","createdAt":"2026-01-30T08:53:25-0500","updatedAt":"2026-01-30T08:54:54-0500","author":{"email":"legacy-642@kitco.com","name":"Reuters","imageUrl":null,"urlAlias":"/author/reuters"},"source":{"id":112,"description":null,"name":"Reuters"},"teaserSnippet":"LONDON, Jan 30 - Gold, silver and copper prices tumbled on ​Friday after hitting record highs this week, as jittery investors moved to lock in ‌profits with hopes for aggressive U.S. interest rate cuts starting to fade and the dollar steadying.President Donald Trump on Friday said he had chosen former Federal Reserve Governor Kevin Warsh to head the U.S. Federal Reserve. The dollar index (.DXY), a measure of the U.S. currency against peers had firmed on expectation of Warsh's ‌appointment.","legacyThumbnailImageUrl":null,"image":{"detail":{"default":{"srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a8c61b15-b8e3-48e2-a4b5-09fed9190dc1.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=1920\u0026token=aecf9139409e7a693a97c91f19bb1375301cb347cc641f082b29a4250becc371"},"sources":{"teaser_small":{"srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a8c61b15-b8e3-48e2-a4b5-09fed9190dc1.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=200\u0026token=3f162c342ab979c0b97c21e8bfbc215c330cc6812e93947dc32ae37326461638","media":"all and (min-width: 0px)"},"teaser_medium":{"srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a8c61b15-b8e3-48e2-a4b5-09fed9190dc1.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=400\u0026token=c5046785e0a604cad5ec6b77163085e661461c1b9eaaf2d95ad26b457f76eb1c","media":"all and (min-width: 0px)"},"desktop":{"media":"all and (min-width: 1024px)","srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a8c61b15-b8e3-48e2-a4b5-09fed9190dc1.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=1920\u0026token=aecf9139409e7a693a97c91f19bb1375301cb347cc641f082b29a4250becc371"},"mobile":{"media":"all and (min-width: 0px)","srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a8c61b15-b8e3-48e2-a4b5-09fed9190dc1.webp?top=0\u0026left=279.8353909465\u0026width=720.329218107\u0026height=720\u0026scale_width=768\u0026token=3f50ca3f7fea878953176b869cc08306911bc59f22df8fd9b7c3133099f33708"},"tablet":{"media":"all and (min-width: 768px)","srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a8c61b15-b8e3-48e2-a4b5-09fed9190dc1.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=1024\u0026token=32ddaa9c947a85f8f9f4fc2c83b772475c87c58e73b73531b9127007bb20d559"}}}},"featuredContent":null,"tags":[],"audioTts":null,"summaryBullets":[]},{"id":216917,"title":"Canada's economic growth stalled in November, could contract in Q4","teaserHeadline":null,"urlAlias":"/news/off-the-wire/2026-01-30/canadas-economic-growth-stalled-november-could-contract-q4","createdAt":"2026-01-30T08:50:19-0500","updatedAt":"2026-01-30T08:51:46-0500","author":{"email":"legacy-642@kitco.com","name":"Reuters","imageUrl":null,"urlAlias":"/author/reuters"},"source":{"id":112,"description":null,"name":"Reuters"},"teaserSnippet":"OTTAWA, Jan 30 (Reuters) - Canada's economic growth stalled in November as growth in services was offset by weakness in goods-producing industries, data showed on Friday, offering fresh clues on the state of the economy after almost a year of tariff and uncertainty.Gross domestic product was flat month-on-month in November, compared with a 0.3% contraction see in October, Statistics Canada said.Analysts polled by Reuters had forecast a marginal 0.1% growth in November.","legacyThumbnailImageUrl":null,"image":{"detail":{"default":{"srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a1b24c45-3549-4749-8ff8-49b0b966f967.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=1920\u0026token=7ca387403b61a048ea98b4b3dc1e80b1a74563f4fcb6f8f7bbd79c22a3dcb815"},"sources":{"teaser_small":{"srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a1b24c45-3549-4749-8ff8-49b0b966f967.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=200\u0026token=9f79dc41ed3565c117dc137d2a2b69325c8717ba0b60b2e9c924d6f0d0ee1753","media":"all and (min-width: 0px)"},"teaser_medium":{"srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a1b24c45-3549-4749-8ff8-49b0b966f967.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=400\u0026token=20b2fb03d57e8b87dd08d95c35a2affc462adf34d7931f61efd12c6c39dc8113","media":"all and (min-width: 0px)"},"desktop":{"media":"all and (min-width: 1024px)","srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a1b24c45-3549-4749-8ff8-49b0b966f967.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=1920\u0026