the $60 a barrel mark this year, as the prospect of oversupply in the market offsets the impact of geopolitical tensions that could disrupt cargoes, a Reuters poll showed on Friday.The survey of 31 economists and analysts conducted in January forecast that Brent crude would average $62.02 per barrel in 2026, slightly up from December's forecast of $61.27. Brent was trading around $70 on January 30 and averaged around $68.20 last year.","legacyThumbnailImageUrl":null,"image":{"detail":{"default":{"srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a38de551-3f2a-4d0d-b3a0-9fa10f80323c.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=1920\u0026token=a4cc24beca2b1b7322f6949364ac48c429e52ceb8d7cd28cc734cabcc3043381"},"sources":{"teaser_small":{"srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a38de551-3f2a-4d0d-b3a0-9fa10f80323c.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=200\u0026token=212eabf94122ea3d43443cc3d99869e5c81450b537bbdb9b9185ce44ee061ca0","media":"all and (min-width: 0px)"},"teaser_medium":{"srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a38de551-3f2a-4d0d-b3a0-9fa10f80323c.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=400\u0026token=23740b87fc21d3b1fec388cc94e85b6a435bdb05a52002fe07baebc79bb63db5","media":"all and (min-width: 0px)"},"desktop":{"media":"all and (min-width: 1024px)","srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a38de551-3f2a-4d0d-b3a0-9fa10f80323c.webp?top=0.16453382084095\u0026left=0\u0026width=1280\u0026height=719.67093235832\u0026scale_width=1920\u0026token=a4cc24beca2b1b7322f6949364ac48c429e52ceb8d7cd28cc734cabcc3043381"},"mobile":{"media":"all and (min-width: 0px)","srcset":"https://image-api.prod.kitco.com/image/a38de551-3f2a-4d0d-b3a0-9fa10f80323c.webp?top=0\u0026left=279.8353909465\u0026width=720.329218107\u0026height=720\u0026scale_width=768\u0026token=a5d45cfe2135881c8fc2059e5f